Subject: [PATCH] configs: an7581: the saved environment sets only the update state

With CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST the environment is the built-in default plus
the listed variables from storage: the two a staged root update keeps between
boots. A saved copy of the boot and update scripts can then never stand in
for the ones this loader was built with.

--- a/include/configs/an7581.h
+++ b/include/configs/an7581.h
@@ -19,0 +20,7 @@
+/*
+ * With CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST, the only variables the saved environment may
+ * set: a staged root update's state. Everything else, the boot and update
+ * scripts first of all, is always the built-in default.
+ */
+#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC	"update_tried:sw,update_failed:sw,loader_tried:sw,loader_failed:sw,loader_booted:sw"
+
